            <ArticleTitle>Pain: a kaleidoscope of ideas, concepts and approaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>173-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The following pages contain summaries and short statements on chronic pain providing further material for reflection and debate, namely: a) synopses of recent findings on: the physiology and biochemistry of pain; the contribution of psychoneuroimmunology; b) some views on a sociology of pain; c) analysis of various concepts and approaches which consider pain as: a symptom of disease a form of behaviour a psychosomatic reaction and a social learning process a communication phenomenon a symptom of disintegrated life a disruption in the integrity of the system a signal of broken unity a breach in the wholeness of the individual; d) a holistic approach in pain therapy; e) some unanswered questions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
